# Mathematics Taste & Wonder Cache
#
# The eternity of proof, Wigner's unreasonable effectiveness, aesthetic inevitability, and Erdős' Book.

#>spw_cache_univ_math_taste
#:cache #!mathematics_taste
#:layer #!pragmatics

^"intent"{
  ~#goal: "Articulate the aesthetic wonder, intellectual immortality, and uncanny physical effectiveness of pure mathematical proof."
  ~#protocol: "cache.layer/1"
}

^"taste_principles"{
  "the_eternal_immutability_of_proof": .{
    immunity_to_falsification: "Unlike empirical natural sciences whose theories are forever provisional and subject to experimental revision, a valid mathematical deduction from chosen axioms is true forever across all possible universes",
    euclidean_timelessness: "Euclid's proof of the infinitude of prime numbers is as pristine, vibrant, and indisputable today as it was in Alexandria 2,300 years ago; it is human civilization's only contact with absolute immortality",
  }[reg=facet],
  "wigners_unreasonable_effectiveness": .{
    miraculous_anticipation_of_physics: "Abstract mathematical structures discovered for pure intellectual delight routinely turn out to be the exact operational language of the physical cosmos: Riemannian non-Euclidean geometry anticipating Einstein's General Relativity, and infinite-dimensional Hilbert spaces anticipating Quantum Mechanics",
    the_universe_as_mathematical_flesh: "The unsettling mystery of why physical reality conforms with sub-atomic precision to the geometric and algebraic daydreams of terrestrial primates",
  }[reg=facet],
  "aesthetic_inevitability_and_the_book": .{
    proofs_from_the_book: "As Paul Erdös envisioned: a supreme proof possesses an undeniable aesthetic economy—stripping away gratuitous calculation to reveal an intuitive, inevitable flash of conceptual light",
    structural_revelation: "Great mathematics does not merely solve an isolated puzzle; it reveals an expansive, previously invisible landscape uniting seemingly unrelated continents of thought",
  }[reg=facet],
}

^"wonder_probes"{
  #>wonder_univ_math_taste_1
  ?["Why did Euler's identity e^(i * pi) + 1 = 0 unite the five fundamental mathematical constants (0, 1, e, pi, i) across analysis, geometry, and arithmetic into a single seven-symbol equation?"]{
    #:depth #!aesthetic ~#lens(transcendental_unification)
    ~#hypothesis: "Euler's identity reveals that rotational angular geometry (pi), exponential calculus growth dynamics (e), algebraic negative inversion (i), additive neutrality (0), and multiplicative unity (1) are not separate mathematical subjects, but orthogonal facets of a single underlying complex analytic manifold."
    !probe{ "Trace the power series expansion of e^(i * theta) = cos(theta) + i * sin(theta) along the complex unit circle to visualize the rotation." }
    $%[analysis.euler_complex_rotation_phase, aesthetics.mathematical_elegance_metric]
  }

  #>wonder_univ_math_taste_2
  ?["How does Gödel's Incompleteness Theorem prove that mathematical truth fundamentally transcends any finite mechanical system of formal proof?"]{
    #:depth #!epistemological ~#lens(truth_transcends_provability)
    ~#hypothesis: "By constructing a self-referential statement G ('This statement cannot be proven within formal system T'), Gödel proved that in any consistent axiomatic system capable of arithmetic, there exist true mathematical statements that cannot be formally derived within the system. Mathematical intuition and human consciousness possess an open-ended semantic grasp of truth that cannot be reduced to closed algorithmic automation."
    !probe{ "Construct the Gödel numbering encoding scheme for self-referential diagonal statements in first-order Peano Arithmetic." }
    $%[logic.godel_arithmetization_code, epistemology.truth_to_provability_gap]
  }
}
